From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:03:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 078/159] [ae-patch] Record each Claude session's account
 beside its status line, and ask Usage for the session's own
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A session on a backup Claude account (a setup token the runner injects) showed
the box's default login's plan limits in the session rail and the usage
popover: nothing recorded which account a session ran on, and the web asked one
host-wide question. The runner now names a backup account in the launch env
(blanking any inherited name), and the statusLine shim writes it to a
claude_account sidecar on every render, empty for the default login, so the AE
relay can key each session's own windows by account. account_label reads an
account's label without loading its token.

The Usage section, the usage popover and the Agents section ask
/v1/ae/limits for their own session and cache each session separately, and the
header names a backup account ("Claude Code · AE Backup").
